<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">National Party of Honduras</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1902</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-party-south-africa">National Party</a> of Honduras is one of the country's two traditional parties, formed in the early twentieth century from the following of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-bonilla">Manuel Bonilla</a>. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiburcio-carias-andino">Tiburcio Carías Andino</a>, who ruled from 1933 to 1949, it dominated the state, and since the return to civilian rule in 1982 it has held the presidency under leaders including Rafael Callejas, Ricardo Maduro, Porfirio Lobo, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-orlando-hernandez">Juan Orlando Hernández</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nasry-asfura">Nasry Asfura</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/national-party-of-honduras.jpg" alt="National Party of Honduras" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kes47 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PNH_2016_logo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
